warofrebellion401unit_djvu.txt | Pettes|Pettis|Pettus | ntest of about twenty minutes the enemy were driven off. One man of Captain McDonald’s company (K) was wounded Avhile at work on the bridge, and has since died. Captain Van Brocklin, having volunteered his services, crossed the river, and, assisted by Captain Pettes with a portion of his company (D), dragged three pontoons across the island and built the bridge across the south branch and the approaches. Ma- • jor Ford reports that extensive swamps bordered the approaches, the river was filled with sunken piles and timbe
