warofrebellion423unit_djvu.txt | pontoon bridge[^.]{0,80}taken  | rom the cavalry sent down the Yaughan road. A squadron of cavalry has just come in from the Bottoway Biver, where they were left by Warren until his column should pass, and then directed to return here collecting stragglers. The commanding officer reports the pontoon bridge over the Bottoway was taken up just before daylight, when he immediately left. He brings in 850 stragglers. He estimates the distance to the bridge twenty miles. He has no news other than above. Saw and heard nothing of the enemy on his return. GEO. G. MEADE, Major- General. City Point, Ya
